  "title": "STN local field potentials from awake Parkinson's disease patients ON and OFF medication, with and without DBS (Wiest et al. 2023)",
  "description": "Local field potentials from the subthalamic nucleus (STN), recorded together with scalp EEG and accelerometry, from patients with Parkinson's disease 3-6 days after DBS surgery while the leads were externalised. Recordings were made OFF and ON dopaminergic medication, at rest and during sessions with 130 Hz STN deep brain stimulation. The data support analysis of how the aperiodic exponent of STN field potentials changes with levodopa and DBS, reflecting excitation/inhibition balance.",
  "methods_description": "STN lead channels (Medtronic, Boston Scientific or Abbott leads) were recorded with TMSi Porti (2048 Hz) or TMSi SAGA32 (4096 Hz) amplifiers alongside scalp EEG and accelerometers, and exported from Spike2 to MATLAB. Stimulation used a custom in-house neurostimulator delivering symmetric biphasic constant-current 130 Hz pulses (60 us) at the middle contacts. Data were converted to BIDS with BrainVision float32 files holding the original values unchanged.",
